{
    "background_story": "Aviana was a majestic bird with iridescent feathers, native to the lush rainforests of South America. She was a member of the Tutsi tribe of birds, known for their vibrant plumage and enchanting songs. Aviana's trills and chirps were said to have healing properties, and the other birds would gather around her to listen in awe. One day, a severe storm ravaged the forest, destroying many nests and leaving the birds homeless. Aviana's Tutsi instincts kicked in, and she took charge, rallying the flock to rebuild and restore their habitat. With her leadership, the birds worked together, using their unique skills to create a thriving community once again. Aviana's selflessness and guidance earned her the title of 'Songstress of the Forest,' and her melodies continued to inspire and uplift the Tutsi tribe.",
